# The rule for this file: anything naming a *build or distribution artifact*
# is anchored to the repository root with a leading slash. Patterns naming a
# tool's own droppings — `__pycache__/`, `.vscode/`, `.idea/` — stay
# recursive on purpose, because those really do appear at every depth. Do not
# "fix" them.
#
# The anchors that are there are load-bearing. A skill is a directory whose
# name is an ordinary English word, so an unanchored `build/` also matches
# `skills/build/` — and it did: the hand-written `build` skill silently could
# not be committed, and CI failed for three pushes on the manifest test that
# requires it. Before adding an unanchored directory pattern, check that it
# cannot collide with a skill name.

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so

# Distribution / packaging.
# `tool.uv.package = false` — this repo builds no sdist or wheel — so these
# only guard against a stray local invocation.
/build/
/dist/
/.eggs/
/*.egg-info/
/*.egg

# Unit test / coverage reports
/htmlcov/
/.coverage
/.coverage.*
/coverage.xml
/.pytest_cache/
/.ruff_cache/

# Virtual environments
/.venv/
/venv/

# Environment
/.python-version
/.env
/.env.*

# IDEs and editors
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Operating systems
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
ehthumbs.db

# Claude
# `.claude/` itself is tracked on purpose — settings.json is shared
# configuration for this repo. Only per-user and scratch state is ignored.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/worktrees

# Proprietary Schuberg Philis content — never vendorable, see README "Not vendored"
skills/sbp-brandbook/
skills/sbp-brandbook
disabled/sbp-brandbook/
disabled/sbp-brandbook
